course: dictionary
lesson: 12629
title: Dismissive: showing you do not care
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dismissive means showing that you think something or someone is not important or not worth your attention. A dismissive person waves away an idea without really listening to it. Look for clues in the way someone speaks, moves or shrugs.
explain: «Mia showed Sam her drawing, but he gave a dismissive shrug and said, "Whatever."» A shrug and "whatever" show that Sam does not think her drawing matters. So dismissive means acting as if something is not worth caring about.
explain: The word can also mean rude in a way that ignores what another person says or feels. «Just get over it» is dismissive of someone's feelings, because it tells them their hurt does not count. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: "Sam gave a not-caring shrug" still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Dismissive means showing that something or someone is not important or not worth your attention.
fact: «A dismissive wave» is a quick hand movement that says the other person is not worth your time.
fact: «Dismissive of» is used with a person's feelings or ideas, as in «He was dismissive of her worries».
fact: Being dismissive of someone's feelings, with words like «just get over it», is unkind.
fact: The adjective changes in comparisons: dismissive, more dismissive, most dismissive.
exercise: «Sam gave a dismissive shrug when Mia asked for help.» What does dismissive mean here? | Showing he was cold | *Showing he did not think her question was important | Showing he was very excited | Showing he was lost
exercise: «The teacher was dismissive of Ben's worry about the test.» Which phrase means nearly the same? | *Brushed it aside as if it did not matter | Read it out loud twice | Wrote it on the board for everyone | Asked him to sit down quietly
exercise: Which of these is a dismissive thing to say to a friend who is upset? | Can I help you with that? | *Just get over it | That sounds really hard | I'm sorry, do you want to talk?
test: «He gave a dismissive wave and carried on reading.» What does the wave show? | Hello, I am very happy to see you | *He did not think the other person was worth his attention | He wanted to dance | He was waving to a friend across the playground
test: Which word is the best synonym for dismissive in «Her dismissive attitude hurt her friends»? | *Uncaring | Excited | Thoughtful | Careful
exam: Why is «just get over it» said to a hurt friend a dismissive comment? | It shows the friend how to be brave | It is a kind way to end a conversation | *It ignores their feelings and makes them feel their hurt does not matter | It asks the friend to write a story
